---
# `safety`, not `production`: this is internal automation for one team, not a
# shared/published role. `production` additionally enforces two purely cosmetic
# style rules this workflow deliberately doesn't follow:
#   - name[template]: would force every task name's Jinja to the end. This role
#     instead leads every task name with "{{ cluster.name }}: ..." on purpose, so
#     ansible-playbook's per-task output is scannable by cluster when multiple
#     clusters run in one invocation.
#   - var-naming[no-role-prefix]: would require every internal fact to be prefixed
#     `onprem_cluster_onboarding_...`. This role instead uses a leading underscore
#     (`_gcloud_auth`, `_rbac_apply`, ...) for role-private facts, Ansible's own
#     documented convention for "internal, don't rely on this from outside."
# All `safety`-tier rules (idempotency, no-changed-when gaps, real correctness
# checks) still apply and must pass clean.
profile: safety
skip_list:
  - yaml[line-length]
  - name[template]
  - var-naming[no-role-prefix]
